  "schema": "finstack_quant.golden/1",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "usd_5y_zcis_self_test",
    "domain": "rates.inflation_swap",
    "description": "Self-test fixture for zero-coupon inflation swap pricing with two-step calibration. Receive-fixed at 2.20% against US-CPI ZCIS for 5Y, 10MM USD notional. Exercises both the discount step (USD-OIS, with ois_compounding override) and the inflation step (US-CPI from 6 ZCIS quotes, against the calibrated discount curve). Closes the inflation calibration step coverage gap (plan \u00a718 follow-up #1).",
    "valuation_date": "2026-04-30",
    "source": "formula",
    "source_detail": "Self-test fixture: 6 ZCIS quotes (1Y-10Y, ~2.0-2.4% rising) calibrate the US-CPI inflation curve against a SOFR OIS-bootstrapped discount curve. Expected outputs captured from Finstack Quant's own calibration + pricing pipeline. Round-trip stability: re-running calibrate + price_instrument_with_metrics must reproduce these values within solver tolerance. Guards regressions in the inflation-step bootstrap, the inflation-swap pricing kernel, and the `inflation` step kind's plumbing through engine::execute. Re-baselined 2026-07-11 after deterministic bootstrap refinements; no external benchmark source is asserted. Re-baselined 2026-09-18, for three reasons. (1) Commit 413953021 anchors a bootstrapped inflation curve at base_date minus the observation lag rather than at base_date, moving the calibrated US-CPI curve and this swap's projected index ratio. (2) The same commit made a historical reference anchor require a published fixing; that guard is deliberate, so the contract now states its base CPI of 300.0 explicitly - the level the plan's US-CPI inflation step declares at its 2026-04-30 base date, i.e. the same start fixing the bootstrap calibrated against. (3) The contract now follows the USD-CPI market convention (one/one accrual, NYSE calendar, modified following, linear monthly reference interpolation), which is what the bootstrap itself reprices against; the 3M observation lag is resolved from the projection curve's indexation_lag_months rather than restated here, and reproduces an explicit override exactly. With the conventions aligned every ZCIS pillar reprices at its own quote to within 1e-5 USD on a 10MM notional (~1e-12 relative), against 8.9e-4 of notional when day count and lag were left mismatched, so this fixture is now a true round-trip test of the inflation bootstrap.",
    "captured_by": "claude",
    "captured_on": "2026-05-09",
    "last_reviewed_by": "claude",
    "last_reviewed_on": "2026-09-18",
    "review_interval_months": 12,
    "regen_command": "uv run pytest finstack-quant-py/tests/golden/test_pricing_inflation_swap.py -v -k self_test",
    "screenshots": []
  },
